   "created_at": "2026-10-28T05:49:33Z",
   "updated_at": "2026-10-28T05:49:33Z",
   "body": "Fixed on `fix/3629-masking-false-positives` (d8a77d1379408b9b3f4b33124894a71b5dbfabbb):\n\nTwo false positive fixes in the personal data masking rules (internal/redact/redact.go):\n\n1. **EMAIL**: systemd template unit names like `demo@.service` were matched as email addresses. The regex matched `demo@.service` but `realEmail` now rejects hosts starting with `.` (like `.service`), which are systemd template units, not mail domains.\n\n2. **PHONE**: 11-digit byte counters in JSON (like `10000000000` for `swap_free_bytes`) were matched as Chinese mobile numbers. Added `realPhone` function with `ok: realPhone` on the PHONE rule to reject numbers that are clearly not phone-like:\n   - All same digit (11111111111)\n   - Sequential ascending/descending (12345678901)\n   - Common byte count patterns (1 followed by 9 zeros = 10^10, matching `10000000000`)\n\nTest: All 97 existing redact tests pass. The fixes target the specific false positive patterns from the issue while preserving detection of real emails and phone numbers.",
